From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ddr: DDR3-1866 calibrates ZQ every 128 ms

The controller ran the long ZQ calibration at initialization only
(ZQCTL0.dis_auto_zq set), so the DRAM's output driver and ODT impedance
were never corrected for temperature and voltage drift afterwards. The SIP
DDR shares the package with the SoC and follows its temperature. Let the
controller issue ZQCS every 128 ms (ZQCTL1, in units of 1024 DFI clocks);
each takes tZQCS = 64 tCK (76 programmed) and blocks that rank only.
---
--- a/plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_config/ddr3_1866_x16/ddrc_init.c
+++ b/plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_config/ddr3_1866_x16/ddrc_init.c
@@ -71,8 +71,10 @@
 	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x114, 0x05050303);
 	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x120, 0x00000907);
 	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x13c, 0x00000000);
-	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x180, 0xC0960026);
-	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x184, 0x00000001);
+	// ZQCTL0: periodic ZQCS (dis_auto_zq off); ZQCL stays off at self-refresh exit.
+	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x180, 0x40960026);
+	// ZQCTL1.t_zq_short_interval_x1024: 0xE3C9 x 1024 DFI clocks = 128 ms at DDR3-1866.
+	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x184, 0x0000E3C9);
 	// phyd related
 	mmio_wr32(0x08004000 + 0x190, 0x048a8305);
 	// DFITMG0.dfi_t_ctrl_delay:24:5:=0x4
